s Chris breaks down how Clive Barker's &quot;Books of Blood&quot; can be used as inspiration in your games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://twincitiebynight.podbean.com/e/episode-329-clive-barkers-books-of-blood/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://d2bwo9zemjwxh5.cloudfront.net/ep-logo/pbblog4577585/Brian_Book_Club_1200x628.jpg?s=fc43cbd3b3f359e34b9f5b5545495142&amp;e=jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twincitiebynight.podbean.com/e/episode-329-clive-barkers-books-of-blood/\" target=\"_blank\"> The Brian Book Club - Clive Barker's \"Books of Blood\" | Twin Cities by Night </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://twincitiebynight.podbean.com/e/episode-329-clive-barkers-books-of-blood/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://twincitiebynight.podbean.com/e/episode-329-clive-barkers-books-of-blood/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Join us as Chris breaks down how Clive Barker's \"Books of Blood\" can be used as inspiration in your games. About the Chronicle Brian&rsquo;s Book Club is a casual, thoughtful series where Chris discusses horror novels, genre fiction, and books that have shaped the tone and themes of Twin Cities by Night&rsquo;s storytelling over the years. Each episode blends personal reflection, literary analysis, and grounded discussion on why certain stories resonate so powerfully within the horror genre. This is not a typical review podcast&mdash;Chris focuses on atmosphere, lessons learned, narrative craft, and the emotional impact of each work. For listeners who enjoy horror, literature, behind-the-scenes creative talk, or discovering new stories that spark inspiration, Brian&rsquo;s Book Club offers a grounded, intimate, and sometimes surprisingly heartfelt experience. \ud83d\udde8\ufe0f Hop into our Discord! Love the stories? Want to chat with the storyteller and players? Or maybe you're just looking for a place to geek out about tabletop roleplaying games? Whether you're a seasoned GM, a curious newbie, or just love hearing epic tales unfold, our community is the perfect place to hang out, ask questions, share your own adventures, and connect with fellow TTRPG fans. Come say hi&mdash;we&rsquo;d love to meet you! \ud83d\udc49 https://discord.gg/T9zeN9p Follow Us X: https://x.com/Twin_Cities_VtM Facebook: https://www.facebook.com/TwinCitiesByNight/ iTunes: https://itunes.apple.com/us/podcast/twin-cities-by-night/id1246523585?mt=2 SoundCloud: https://soundcloud.com/twin-cities-by-night YouTube: https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCBUyj7h-xIhwsM3kHK56SRA </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> The Brian Book Club is a series when we cover different horror stories in all media forms, and how you can be inspired by them to run and play in World of Darkness games. World of Darkness and its game settings are owned by White Wolf Publishing.<br /> <br /> If you would like to support the podcast stop by our Patreon<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/TwinCitiesbyNight\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.patreon.com/TwinCitiesbyNight</a><br /> <br /> Come by and visit our Discord!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/T9zeN9p\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/T9zeN9p\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://discord.gg/T9zeN9p\" target=\"_blank\"> https://discord.gg/T9zeN9p </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Check us out on iTunes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://itunes.apple.com/us/podcast/twin-cities-by-night/id1246523585?m